This software is source-available, not open source. The code is published so
that you can read it, verify what it does with your medical records, and run
it yourself. It is not placed in the public domain and it is not licensed for
redistribution.


1. DEFINITIONS

   "The Software" means the source code, documentation, build scripts and
   packaged applications published under this licence.

   "The Author" means Noelle Bhaduri.

   "Personal Use" means use by a natural person, for their own records or the
   records of members of their household or family for whom they are
   responsible, with no fee charged and no commercial benefit sought.


2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   a. Read, study and audit the source code, in full, for any purpose.

   b. Download, install and run the Software for Personal Use, on any number
      of devices you control.

   c. Modify the Software, and run your modified copy, for Personal Use.

   d. Make copies for backup, and move your copy between your own devices.

   e. Quote excerpts of the source code in reviews, security reports,
      educational material, articles and academic work, with attribution.


