6. NOT MEDICAL ADVICE, NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE

   Health Ledger is a filing cabinet. It stores, organises and prints records
   that already exist. It does not diagnose, treat, cure or prevent anything,
   and it is not a substitute for professional medical advice.

   It has not been reviewed or approved by the FDA, the MHRA, the EMA, or any
   other regulator, and it is not certified as a medical device anywhere.

   The pharmacogenomic and genetic reference tables in the Software are
   compiled from public sources. A gene or variant being named correctly is
   not the same as it being safe to act on. Nothing the Software shows you is
   a reason to start, stop or change a medication. Talk to your doctor or
   pharmacist.


